hey guys pete here today i'm going to  talk more about dark season 3.  they updated the official dark website  with a modified version of the painting  that adam has hanging in the sick mundus  lair  that brings up some interesting  questions and actually ties in  with an update i wanted to add to my  last season 3 theories video  also they added the phrase the end is  the beginning to the home page which  isn't new  but i have been thinking about it and  want to discuss it before we get going  though this video will contain spoilers  if you're not into that sort of thing or  aren't caught up through the end of  season 2  then this video won't be something  you're gonna want to watch i will  mention spoilery photos from behind the  scenes of filming season 3 that are out  there  and there was a bit of confirmation  information that leaked out in relation  to the website update but i won't  mention that until the very end  netflix has posted an official  description for season 3 since i last  made a video  it reads in the third and final season  dark  reaches its mind-bending conclusion  moving beyond the concept of space and  time  upon arrival in a new world jonas tries  to make sense of what this rendition of  vindin means for his own  fate while the ones left behind in the  other world  are left on a quest to break the loop  that now not only bends  time but also space two worlds light and  dark  and in the center a tragic love story of  epic proportions  this isn't giving a lot away it lines up  with our expectations  that jonas will spend time in the  alternate world where he presumably  traveled with alt martha at the end of  season 2.  the ones who are left behind most likely  refers to the group of survivors in the  bunker  we know that claudio will be  experimenting with the god particle  and that noah and elizabeth will get  together with the latter giving birth to  her own mother  charlotte it's interesting how they  emphasize the epic love story at the  center of things  i'm reminded of a long form interview i  watched with the showrunners last year  where they brought that  up it's funny because as a viewer i  spent so much time trying to figure out  how everything works that i forget that  the star-crossed relationship between  jonas and marta is foundational to the  story they're telling us  the last bit two worlds light and dark  is a perfect transition into the  painting in the background of the  official website  the original piece is the one we've seen  under the church in adam's  lair it's named the fall of the damned  or  the fall of the rebel angels and it was  painted by  peter paul rubens rubens was an  influential flemish painter  from the baroque movement it's a 17th  century  religious painting that depicts the  archangel michael expelling lucifer and  the rebel angels from heaven we see the  archangel at the top  in the light section of the painting  that represents heaven and see the  angels falling towards the dark  as they fall we see their flesh being  torn away by demonic looking creatures  the version of the painting on the  website has several additions related to  the series  in the middle we see jonas in a  radiation suit  these suits are connected to the god  particle time machine in the power plant  so it seems likely that we will see him  visit that  in season three above him we see a  pregnant woman in white  the first guess of who this was was  ennis conwald because there's a  resemblance  she is jonas's grandmother we know that  before she adopted mikhail  she had a child of her own that died at  a very young age  we don't really know the details about  that which leaves some fans wondering if  there's more  to be learned there the other popular  idea of who this might be  is related to a behind-the-scenes photo  that the actor who plays celia  posted and then deleted from her  instagram it's pretty hard not to make a  connection here but we don't know much  about the photo itself  in the reddit post i saw there was an  explanation that the actor had removed  the photo  and there was a related shot of lisa  bakari who plays alt marta  that might be on the same couch  indicating that it came from the set  i don't know i always imagined celia  would be connected in some way or the  other but i guess because of the age we  meet her  at i assumed it would be as someone's  child rather than a parent  next we have what looks like an  alt-world tan house to me he's a  character we know wears glasses  and the device he's with looks like it's  time travel machine related  the only problem is that in prime linden  he has dark hair  as a young man but so far the strategy  appears to be  to mark the alt-world versions with  something to set them apart  if this is ton house it raises a lot of  questions about the evolution of the  time machines  but doesn't provide any answers there is  a spherical object involved which brings  alt marta's device to mind but we'll  have to wait and see what's going on  here  from what we see we can't really deduce  what stage of the development of the  machines this would be  below him there's another pregnant woman  whose face is obscured completely this  could literally be anybody at this point  as there's nothing that's recognizable  as far as i can tell  not far from her we have marta and the  yellow raincoat what stands out most  about her  image is that she's definitely in the  dark portion of the  painting but not necessarily in the pit  of hell visually she's closer to the  dark elements  sort of on the border while jonas above  her is closer to the light elements  this may be indicating that venden prime  is the light world from the season 3  description  which would make sense since that's  where the story started  beyond that you can't make out much  about her other than she looks  distressed  next the new character trio is on the  bottom left of the painting and they  look like they're firmly in the pit of  hell they don't look out of place there  or  in any way distressed about it i  wouldn't say this does much in the way  of solving the mystery of who this  character  is i still believe it's the same person  at three different points in their life  working together and if anything this  just reinforces that they're probably a  dark force  that you wouldn't want to come in  contact with above them is the character  from the season 3 data announcement  trailer who's wearing the pink jacket  and beating someone with a rock  this was something that i wanted to  update from my last video  because reddit discovered that her name  tag had been digitally  changed to read helene albert there was  a theory based on one of the behind the  scenes photos that she was katarina's  mother which i wasn't sold on initially  part of where that skepticism came from  was her name being named helene wolfe  so learning that they went back and  changed it is a pretty big deal  based on in-world documents we know that  katarina's maiden name was albert  this connects her to the character who  aegon visited about the sheep dying his  name was listed in the credits as  heremon  albert so it's been assumed that he's  katarina's father  changing the name tag that's something  that had to happen for a reason  and the only thing that really makes  sense is that this woman is katarina's  mother  who she's hitting with the rock and why  she's important enough to be included in  this painting is still a mystery though  the one low-key addition to this is an  edit of a couple having sex right in the  middle  the woman appears to have dark hair with  bangs which makes you wonder if it's alt  marta and jonas  but we can't really make out the man so  it's not really clear  it's painted on top of a character that  was in the original  and beyond that i'm not sure what to  make of it the final two additions are  both a little strange  on the left side claudius poodle  gretchen has been added  this seems like a bit of fun more than  anything else but we'll see  above her in heaven we see bowler with  no eye injury there has been some  discussion that this might be stranger  jonas based on the images we've seen of  him in the past but i don't see it  there's this behind the scene shot of  roller with a beard that looks like a  closer match to me  does that mean moeller has a big role to  play in season 3  maybe or this could just be the  showrunners continuing to have fun with  the mystery about his eye  that's the last of the added images and  that brings us to the title  when you visit the site you see the word  dark and then the phrase the end is the  beginning  comes across the screen after that it  says discover how everything is the same  but different  the last part refers to the two worlds  light and dark  and jonas making sense of what that all  means the end is the beginning is not a  new phrase in relation to the series but  now that we're at the end it's worth  thinking about  the shorthand ideas he posted everywhere  is that the series will  end right back where it started the  beginning like season 1  episode 1. i get the novelty behind this  and then it might be satisfying because  it would be in line with causal  determinism  i do wonder though how entertaining that  might be considering that not everyone  who watches  and enjoys this show does so because  they like thinking about how time travel  might work in practice  there almost has to be something  character driven behind it it has to  matter that nothing can change and it  should make us feel something or we  should be able to connect to it  in a way that moves us and what does  that look like  the end being the beginning other than  watching michael get ready to hang  himself  does it imply that jonas as adam would  just die  failing to do anything meaningful as a  result of his decades of effort  and don't get me wrong i like a good  tragedy and i do have faith that if they  went this route they would bake in some  sort of catharsis  i'm just curious about what that would  be i'm interested in hearing what you  guys think about that in the comments  i can't imagine a scenario where  whatever adam and or claudia is trying  to do  turns out to be the trigger for what  we've seen so far  but it raises a crazy amount of  questions so let me know what you think  the last thing i want to talk about  before i go is the leaked information  from the website i mentioned  i don't think any of it is really  shocking or even game changing  but i thought i should wait until the  end if you wanted to avoid it  when the site was updated reddit user  t-i-r-a-c-o  posted a javascript file that they found  inside that they noticed that the site  will start displaying information for  characters in two worlds which are  labeled a  and b i doubt this is surprising to  anyone at this point but it is notable  that there are only two  worlds overall this just means when you  look up a character you'll be able to  view information on the original and  alternate versions  the only three names discovered in  relation to world b  were marta magnus and mads without any  additional context as far as i can tell  since they're all names to start with  the letters m a  i'm not reading too much into that  there's obviously other characters that  live in that world there's also a  reference to the year 1888  in world a that shows up in season 3  episode 2.  again we pretty much knew stranger would  end up in that year  but this does seem to confirm it finally  the year 2003 from world a shows up on  jonas's timeline i was hoping that we  would see different years  and this seems to confirm that it's not  really clear jonas may have been born in  2003  if he was only supposed to be 16 when we  first met him but i've also seen that  they cast a child  actor to play him at a younger age and  we don't know anything else about that  it'll be interesting to see how this all  ties into the ending and i suppose this  would be a good place to end the video  let me know what you think in the  comments and please like this video if  you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already i'll be doing more dark  videos weekly until season 3 is released  thanks for watching i will talk to you  soon

